    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n390" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac-commŏdus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adc.</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>fit</i>, <i>suitable</i> (vox Verg. and <b>poet.</b> for <i>adcommodatus</i>);
			with <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valles adcommoda fraudi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 522</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membra bellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 4, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nox fraudi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Theb. 10, 192</span></i>
			.— Also in late prose, Cod. Th. 15, 1, 41;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Jul. 8, 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. 4, 2, 12
				al.</span></i>—<i>Comp.</i>, <i>sup.</i>, and adv. not found.</div>
